{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Problems and Solutions"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Finally, We Got It!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.  Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.  Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le12ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Expressing Certainty About Conditions:<span class=\"italic\"> If </span>and <span class=\"italic\">When"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to talk about the certainty of a condition, you can use the first conditional with<span class=\"italic\"> if </span>and <span class=\"italic\">when. You use the first conditional to refer to events, actions or situations that are possible in the present or the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the first conditional, you have to be careful of which word (if or when) you use. The use of each implies a different meaning."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If </span>you have some time this afternoon, will you please send me a copy of the confirmation? "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">If </span>implies a less certain meaning. In this sentence, the condition of <span class=\"italic\">If you have some time this afternoon</span> implies that the speaker is not sure if the person has some time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I will send it to you <span class=\"strong\">when</span> I get back to the office."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">When</span> implies a more certain meaning. In this sentence, <span class=\"italic\">when I get back to the office</span> implies that the speaker is quite certain that they will return to the office."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take a look at some more examples from the text:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we provide itemized receipts, all other expenses will be covered as well."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we tip a cab driver, we won't really be able to get a receipt."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I suppose we will receive our conference badges when we check in, right?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Perfect Infinitives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Infinitives are a common grammar point to use in English. You can use them in a variety of forms and with different verbs. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Perfect infinitive when the action of the infinitive has already taken place."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">seem to have enjoyed </span>your vacation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The action (enjoy your vacation) took place in the past. The observer is noticing something about that event and is commenting on it in the present. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of the perfect infinitive is:<br> verb + to have infinitive <br><span class=\"italic\">  I'm <span class=\"strong\">glad to have made</span> your day, Adam."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We were smart to have submitted such a detailed proposal."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Weren't were supposed to have heard about the conference by now? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It would be disappointing to have written that whole proposal only to have the request denied."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Kristi was supposed to have told you."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to look over "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to review"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Would you like to look it over?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to discuss a proposal."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to give something a once-over "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to review something quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's give it a once-over, just to make sure everything is in order."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "requisition "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to officially request something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Were all of our requisitions accepted?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go over with a fine-tooth comb "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to review something thoroughly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They really went over it with a fine-tooth comb."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "per diem "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an amount of money allotted for spending each day"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did we get our per diem?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "itemized receipt "}, 